                <pb facs="1049" n="891" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg891"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Furniss to
                        the Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Port au
                                Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-11-08"><hi rendition="#italic">November 8,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 122.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am in receipt of department’s No. 46 of
                    October 23, 1906, and am pleased to state that the case therein mentioned was
                    settled agreeable to my contentions, as stated in my No. 115 of October 30,
                    1906.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. W. Furniss.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
